# Web SPA dev env stub (owned by web-fsd-rework — DEC-002 / DEC-008).
#
# No custom VITE_* keys are required. The SPA uses only Vite built-ins:
#   - import.meta.env.BASE_URL — BrowserRouter basename ("/" for login at root)
#   - import.meta.env.DEV — API URL dual-mode
#       (dev: relative "/api" via Vite proxy → 127.0.0.1:8100;
#        prod: same-origin "/api/..." via nginx → Nest)
#
# Compose `web` loads this file via env_file so the path exists. An empty
# key list is valid. Runtime env_file does NOT rewrite baked static assets.
#
# Before `docker compose ... up --watch`, copy:
#   copy web\.env.dev.example web\.env.dev   (Windows)
#   cp web/.env.dev.example web/.env.dev     (Unix)
#
# API/db secrets live in backend/.env.dev —
# see ../backend/.env.dev.example.
# Compose SPA: http://localhost:8090/  (login at root)
# Host Vite: npm run dev in web/ (built-ins only; no custom env required).
